This project grew out of a local Antigravity adapter and observation UI developed
while extending PAL MCP Server 9.8.2 (BeehiveInnovations/pal-mcp-server), upstream
commit 7afc7c1cc96e23992c8f105f960132c657883bb1, licensed under Apache-2.0.
Upstream: https://github.com/BeehiveInnovations/pal-mcp-server

The standalone package does not bundle the PAL server, its provider integrations,
the Antigravity CLI binary, or any authentication material. Its bounded process
capture and public-event history were extracted from our local PAL adaptation;
configuration, MCP tools, monitor lifecycle, packaging, and portable tests were
rewritten for this standalone distribution. The original Apache-2.0 license is
included. No affiliation with Google, Antigravity, OpenAI, or the PAL maintainers
is implied.

Version 0.8.0 restores the command-builder/parser separation and Claude/Codex
message extraction concepts from PAL's clink/agents and clink/parsers (same
upstream revision). They are adapted to bounded streaming, explicit channel and
participant provenance, strict terminal-state validation and the standalone
discussion store. PAL's permissive Claude/Codex default arguments, raw-event
retention and recovery of unsuccessful CLI runs are intentionally not retained.
